  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When an egg is boiled, the soluble globular protein, albumin present in it is converted to insoluble fibrous protein. </p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During denaturation, its biological activity is lost. Boiling an egg causes denaturation of its protein resulting in loss of its quaternary, tertiary and secondary structures.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">But the primary structure (representing the sequence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi></math> amino acids) remains intact.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hence option A is the answer.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
